        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to introduce 102A Carrow Road, Drimnagh, Dublin 12 —a beautifully presented four-bedroom, two-bathroom end of terrace home, offering approximately 92 sq.m of well-appointed living space.\nUpon entry, an entrance hallway provides access to a downstairs bathroom fitted with a bath/shower, WC, and hand basin. The hallway also leads to the front living room, which features a fireplace. From here, double doors open into a fully fitted open-plan dining and kitchen area, with access to the rear outdoor space.\n\nThe first floor comprises four rooms, including two bedrooms that share an en-suite bathroom and one single room. The landing also provides access to an attic space.\n102A Carrow Road is situated in Drimnagh, a residential area in Dublin 12. The street is quiet and mainly lined with terraced and semi-detached homes, making it a family-friendly neighbourhood.\n\nThe area benefits from good transport links, with several Dublin Bus routes nearby and the Drimnagh Luas Red Line stop within walking distance, providing easy access to the city centre. Local amenities, including shops, cafés, and services, are available in surrounding districts such as Rialto, Kilmainham, Crumlin, and Kimmage.\n\nThere are also green spaces nearby, including Brickfield Park and Lansdowne Valley Park, which offer opportunities for walking and recreation. Overall, Drimnagh is considered a settled and community-oriented area, combining suburban calm with convenient access to the wider city.\n\nDon't miss out on this fantastic opportunity. Early viewing is highly recommended! Call RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS today for further information.\n\nFeatures;\n<ul>\n <li>c. 92 sq.m</li>\n <li>BER C1</li>\n <li>4 Bed/ 2 Bath</li>\n <li>End of terrace home</li>\n <li>Private driveway</li>\n <li>No onward chain</li>\n <li>Fantastic condition throughout</li>\n <li>Positioned within a quiet cul de sac</li>\n <li>Mature well-established neighbourhood</li>\n <li>The LUAS stop within minutes from your doorstep</li>\n <li>Wide range of local shops & amenities close by</li>\n <li>Prime for first-time buyers, investors or anyone looking to trade up</li>\n <li>Viewing highly advised!</li>\n</ul>\n\nDirections;\nFrom the M50, take the Red Cow exit onto Naas Road toward Dublin, turn right onto Davitt Road, then right onto Kilworth Road, and left onto Carrow Road; 102A will be on the left."
      },
